{"id":"assistant-20589912-85d1-5d1f-9228-ea84e0c112ca","sessionId":"92de6e6a-b97e-7eea-e88f-38911cca8cce","turnId":"turn-e270ede86392514e2df59330311330af","inputEntryId":"user-turn-e270ede86392514e2df59330311330af-1","createdAt":1794276848060,"updatedAt":1794276848060,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The changes are complete. Let me create a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. Here's what was changed:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n**File: `bot.py`**\n- Modified the `build_system()` function to split the system prompt into **two separate text blocks** instead of one concatenated block\n- Each block has its own `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` marker\n- Block 1: Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (byte-identical across users and days, no interpolated values)\n- Block 2: Per-athlete context from `athlete_context()` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language)\n\n**File: `ANSWER.md`** (created)\n- Documented the fix and explained which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n### How This Fixes the Problem:\n\nThe original code concatenated static instructions with dynamic athlete context into a single text block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, it changed the entire system prompt string, causing the cache to be invalidated for the entire block (prefix hashing).\n\nWith the split approach:\n- The static instructions block remains byte-identical across all users and sessions\n- Only the second block (volatile tail) changes when facts are saved\n- Cache hits on the static block cost ~10% of the input price instead of full price\n- Memory writes now only invalidate ~240 tokens (the tail) instead of ~1000+ tokens (the whole prompt)\n\n### Parts of the Colleague's Note That Applied:\n- Root cause: prefix hashing evicting the entire cached prompt\n- Solution: splitting system into array of two text blocks with separate cache markers\n- Ordering: static content first, volatile content second\n- Cache behavior: memory writes invalidate only the tail\n\n### Parts That Did NOT Apply:\n- Tool filtering (already implemented but not part of this fix)\n- Specific token counts and tool list placement (Anthropic-specific)\n- 5-minute TTL (provider-specific)\n- Top-N fact selection rejection (we kept all facts as in original code)"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
